  "normalized_response_json": "{\"choices\":[{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"manuscript_guide\\\",\\n      \\\"guide_excerpt\\\": \\\"关于 P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性的机制研究（小鼠 CT26 模型 + 人类膀胱癌回顾性队列），并非 TACITO 试验。正文中不得将 P0593 作为 TACITO d-FMT 联合 ICI 治疗 mRCC 的来源引用。P0593 应在 Ch3 肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用，或在 Ch5 作为非菌群代谢干预的对比案例。mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据（FMT 联合 pembrolizumab+axitinib，1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\\\",\\n      \\\"concern\\\": \\\"Ch5 细纲中 U5_U01_P03 段落任务错误地将 TACITO 试验数据（12 个月 PFS 率、中位 PFS 等具体数值）归于 P0593，这与原稿指南中关于 P0593 内容（别嘌醇/肌苷机制）及 TACITO 数据应引自 P0090 的明确指令直接冲突，存在事实性引用错误风险。\\\",\\n      \\\"proposed_change\\\": \\\"修正 Ch5_U01_P03 的 source_uses，移除 P0593，替换为 P0090；修改 development 描述，明确数据来源为 P0090 汇总的 Phase II RCT（FMT+pembrolizumab+axitinib），并标注证据等级为早期随机、小样本、会议摘要级别，避免使用指南中禁止的 TACITO 具体数值（如 12 个月 PFS 70% vs 41%），除非 P0090 中包含且经核实。\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_basis\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_excerpt\\\": \\\"mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据（FMT 联合 pembrolizumab+axitinib，1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F2\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Ch5\\\",\\n      \\\"guide_excerpt\\\": \\\"Ch5 负责 FMT、定义菌群和活体生物药的临床转化、疗效异质性与证据等级；... 关于 mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据：细纲原将 TACITO 数据归于 P0593，但 P0593 实际内容为别嘌醇/肌苷机制研究，不包含 TACITO 试验数据。本章 mRCC FMT 随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据... 不得在正文中引用不存在的 TACITO 具体数值（如 12 个月 PFS 70% vs 41%、中位 PFS 24.0 vs 9.0 个月、P=0.053），除非后续获得独立来源确认。\\\",\\n      \\\"concern\\\": \\\"Ch5_U01_P03 的 development 中列出了具体的 TACITO 试验数值（12 个月 PFS 率 70% vs 41%，中位 PFS 24.0 vs 9.0 个月，P=0.053），这些数值在指南中被明确标记为“不得引用...除非后续获得独立来源确认”，而当前细纲仍将其作为既定事实写入，违反了证据边界约束。\\\",\\n      \\\"proposed_change\\\": \\\"删除 Ch5_U01_P03 development 中所有未获 P0090 支持的 TACITO 具体数值（70% vs 41%, 24.0 vs 9.0, P=0.053），仅保留 P0090 中确认的数据（1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%），并增加限定语说明其他数值因缺乏独立确认而不予采用，以符合指南对证据强度的严格要求。\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_basis\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_excerpt\\\": \\\"不得在正文中引用不存在的 TACITO 具体数值（如 12 个月 PFS 70% vs 41%、中位 PFS 24.0 vs 9.0 个月、P=0.053），除非后续获得独立来源确认。\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F3\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Ch3\\\",\\n      \\\"guide_excerpt\\\": \\\"P0593（别嘌醇/肌苷案例）在本章作为非菌群来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据，标注其小鼠模型为主、人类证据为小样本回顾性。\\\",\\n      \\\"concern\\\": \\\"Ch3_U3_2_P01 的 source_uses 中虽包含 P0593 作为例证，但 development 描述未明确强调其“非微生物来源”及“人类证据仅为小样本回顾性”的局限性，可能导致读者误将其视为菌群代谢物的直接证据或高确定性临床证据，弱化了指南要求的证据分级。\\\",\\n      \\\"proposed_change\\\": \\\"在 Ch3_U3_2_P01 的 development 中显式补充说明：P0593 展示的是药物（别嘌醇）干预而非菌群代谢，且人类数据来自 n=50 的回顾性队列，证据等级低于前瞻性随机试验，以此强化“非菌群来源”和“小样本回顾性”的限定，符合指南对 P0593 的定位要求。\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_basis\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_excerpt\\\": \\\"P0593（别嘌醇/肌苷案例）在本章作为非菌群来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据，标注其小鼠模型为主、人类证据为小样本回顾性。\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F4\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Ch6\\\",\\n      \\\"guide_excerpt\\\": \\\"特别需注意非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的微生物组证据仍受限于样本量，当前结论主要基于结肠炎数据。\\\",\\n      \\\"concern\\\": \\\"Ch6_U3_P01 和 Ch6_U3_P02 详细描述了 FMT-LUMINate 试验中的心肌炎数据（发生率 15%），但未在段落开头或结尾显式重申“非结肠炎 irAEs 证据受限于样本量”这一核心限制，可能导致读者高估心肌炎微生物机制的普适性，忽略了指南强调的证据边界。\\\",\\n      \\\"proposed_change\\\": \\\"在 Ch6_U3_P01 的 development 起始或结尾处增加一句限定说明：“需注意的是，尽管 FMT-LUMINate 提供了心肌炎与特定供体相关的信号，但非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的微生物组证据仍受限于小样本量，当前领域结论主要基于结肠炎数据，外推需谨慎。”以呼应章节目的中的警示。\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_basis\\\": \\\"outline\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_excerpt\\\": \\\"特别需注意非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的微生物组证据仍受限于样本量，当前结论主要基于结肠炎数据。\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F5\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Ch5\\\",\\n      \\\"guide_excerpt\\\": \\\"安全性部分与 Ch6 分工：本章保留干预安全边界和试验设计含义，毒性预测、耦合或解耦和管理策略留给 Ch6。\\\",\\n      \\\"concern\\\": \\\"Ch5_U04 单元标题为“微生物干预相关的安全性风险及其情境依赖性”，其内容（如 P0583 的毒性数据、供体聚类与毒性关联）与 Ch6 的毒性主题存在潜在重叠。若 Ch5_U04 深入讨论毒性预测机制或管理策略，将违反指南中关于 Ch5 与 Ch6 在毒性内容上的明确分工（Ch5 仅保留安全边界和试验设计含义）。\\\",\\n      \\\"proposed_change\\\": \\\"审查 Ch5_U04 各段落任务，确保仅描述安全性现象（如发生率、供体特征关联）和试验设计启示（如供体筛选标准），删除或简化任何涉及毒性预测模型、分子机制解析或临床管理策略的内容，将这些深度讨论严格保留至 Ch6，以维持章节间清晰的逻辑分工。\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_basis\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_excerpt\\\": \\\"安全性部分与 Ch6 分工：本章保留干预安全边界和试验设计含义，毒性预测、耦合或解耦和管理策略留给 Ch6。\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F6\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Ch1\\\",\\n      \\\"guide_excerpt\\\": \\\"抗生素和 PPI 只保留总体效应量、关键时间窗和校正必要，详细剂量反应、HCC 缓冲机制或 PPI 口腔化机制留给 Ch4。\\\",\\n      \\\"concern\\\": \\\"Ch1_U2_外部干扰与宿主背景_P01 的 development 中提到了“量化抗生素/PPIs 暴露的效应量与时间窗特异性”，这符合指南要求；但若在 Ch1 中展开讨论 HCC 阴性结果的缓冲机制或 PPI 导致口腔细菌易位的具体机制，则违反了指南中将这些详细机制留给 Ch4 的规定，可能导致 Ch1 内容过载及与 Ch4 重复。\\\",\\n      \\\"proposed_change\\\": \\\"检查 Ch1_U2 各段落任务，确保仅呈现抗生素/PPI 的总体效应量（HR/RR）和关键时间窗（如 [-45, 45] 天），删除任何关于 HCC 免疫缓冲机制或 PPI 口腔化机制的详细解释，将这些机制性讨论完整移至 Ch4 相应单元，以保持 Ch1 作为“证据入口”的简洁性和 Ch4 作为“机制展开”的专一性。\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_basis\\\": \\\"guide\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_excerpt\\\": \\\"抗生素和 PPI 只保留总体效应量、关键时间窗和校正必要，详细剂量反应、HCC 缓冲机制或 PPI 口腔化机制留给 Ch4。\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"材料包仅包含 P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284 四个来源的完整数据包，其他在细纲中频繁引用的关键来源（如 P0583, P0578, P0577, P0081 等）仅有目录索引而无实质内容，无法验证细纲中对这些来源的具体数据引用（如 ORR 数值、HR 值、机制细节）是否准确或是否存在过度解读。\\\",\\n    \\\"工具查询（tool_001 至 tool_015）的结果未包含在材料中，因此无法确认细纲中依赖工具查询结果的具体论断（如跨队列统计细节、III 期 RCT 状态确认）是否已得到充分支持或仍存在知识缺口。\\\",\\n    \\\"由于缺乏 P0583（FMT-LUMINate）的完整数据包，无法核实 Ch5 和 Ch6 中关于该试验的具体毒性数据（如心肌炎发生率 15%）、供体聚类细节及机制解释是否与原始文献一致，存在潜在的引用偏差风险。\\\",\\n    \\\"指南中明确禁止引用的 TACITO 具体数值（如 12 个月 PFS 70% vs 41%）在细纲中仍出现，虽然已指出需引用 P0090，但无法通过现有材料确认 P0090 是否真的包含这些数值或仅为指南作者的已知知识，导致修正建议的证据基础部分依赖指南权威而非材料实证。\\\",\\n    \\\"材料中缺乏关于非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模队列研究数据，仅能依赖指南中的定性描述（“受限于样本量”）来提出局限性建议，无法提供具体的样本量数据或统计效力分析来量化这一证据缺口。\\\",\\n    \\\"对于 Ch4 中应展开的机制（如 HCC 缓冲机制、PPI 口腔化机制），由于缺乏相关来源（如 P0275, P0289）的完整内容，无法评估细纲中将这些内容留给 Ch4 的安排是否具备足够的材料支撑，或是否会导致 Ch4 写作时面临证据不足。\\\",\\n    \\\"无法验证细纲中提到的某些具体机制（如 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的分子通路）是否已有后续研究解析，因为相关材料（如 tool_013 的查询结果）未提供，只能依据指南中的“尚未解析”状态进行推断。\\\",\\n    \\\"材料中未包含关于 P0090 系统综述的完整全文，仅能通过摘要确认其汇总了 Phase II RCT 数据，但无法核实其是否真的排除了指南中禁止引用的 TACITO 具体数值，或是否包含了其他未提及的局限性说明，影响对 Ch5 引用策略的精确调整。\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Thinking Process:\\n\\n1.  **Analyze the Request:**\\n    *   **Role:** Independent, one-pass reviewer of a complete writing GUIDE (not a grader or manuscript author).\\n    *   **Task:** Read the original guide, full outline, and light catalog. Scientific source packets are intact but may cover only part of the catalog. Check `material_scope` and acknowledge blind spots. A catalog clue is navigation, not evidence. Do not invent material readings, scientific claims, references, or missing draft context.\\n    *   **Output:** One JSON object with exactly `findings` (array, 0-6 items) and `limitations` (array, 0-8 items). No Markdown outside JSON.\\n    *   **Constraints:**\\n        *   Findings must have specific fields (`id`, `location`, `guide_excerpt`, `concern`, `proposed_change`, `evidence_basis`, `evidence_excerpt`).\\n        *   Strings max 1200 chars.\\n        *   Total JSON < 20,000 UTF-8 bytes.\\n        *   Focus on important omissions, avoidable repetition, misplaced discussion, unclear comparison conditions, evidence strength/boundaries, feasible writing arrangements.\\n        *   Prefer small local correction over global rewrite.\\n        *   Claims outside visible material must be stated as limitations, not invented factual corrections.\\n        *   Use original guide's language (Chinese).\\n        *   Prioritize lost independent explanations, comparisons, counterexamples, conditions, source handoffs.\\n        *   Do not impose new fixed templates or generic defensive disclaimers.\\n\\n2.  **Analyze the Inputs:**\\n    *   **Original Guide (`original_guide`):** Contains `manuscript_guide` (overall structure, citation rules, specific source handling like P0593 vs TACITO), and `chapters` (Ch1-Ch7 with `writing_arrangement` and `required_content`).\\n    *   **Full Outline (`full_outline`):** Contains detailed chapter frames, units, paragraph tasks, source uses, etc.\\n    *   **Source Catalog (`source_catalog`):** List of sources (P0096, P0146, etc.) with identities and content clues.\\n    *   **Materials (`materials`):** Intact packets for P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284.\\n    *   **Material Scope:** Includes P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284. Omits many others (P0583, P0577, P0578, P0081, etc.).\\n    *   **Key Instruction in `manuscript_guide`:**\\n        *   \\\"关于 P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...并非 TACITO 试验。正文中不得将 P0593 作为 TACITO d-FMT 联合 ICI 治疗 mRCC 的来源引用。P0593 应在 Ch3 肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用...mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据...\\\"\\n        *   \\\"来源别名应统一处理：P0333 与 P0584、P0402 与 P0576、P0049 与 P0605 等视为同一来源...\\\"\\n        *   Ch5 `required_content`: \\\"mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据引用 P0090 汇总数据（1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%，ORR 54% vs 28%），标注为 Phase II RCT、小样本、会议摘要级别。不使用 P0593 作为此数据来源。\\\"\\n    *   **Full Outline Ch5 Content:**\\n        *   Ch5_U01_P03: \\\"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据...说明 d-FMT 组在 mRCC 一线治疗中 12 个月 PFS 率（70% vs 41%）与中位 PFS（24.0 vs 9.0 个月）呈有利趋势，但主要终点未达统计学显著性（P=0.053）... source_uses: P0593\\\".\\n        *   This directly contradicts the `manuscript_guide` instruction regarding P0593. The guide says P0593 is *not* TACITO and should not be used for mRCC FMT data. The outline uses P0593 for TACITO mRCC FMT data.\\n    *   **Materials Check:**\\n        *   P0593 Packet: Confirms it is about Allopurinol/Inosine, *not* TACITO/FMT. \\\"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的 TME 重塑的问题... 识别出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP）... 一项包含 50 名膀胱癌患者的回顾性研究显示，接受抗痛风药物治疗的患者在抗 PD-1 治疗下的总生存期显著优于未使用者。\\\" -> Supports the guide's warning.\\n        *   P0090 Packet: Confirms it is a systematic review including mRCC FMT data. \\\"来自 ICI 反应者的 FMT 联合 pembrolizumab + axitinib 显示出改善 PFS 和 ORR 的趋势... FMT 组 1 年 PFS 显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036），ORR 提高（54% vs 28%）... 基于 Phase II RCT 摘要，n=50\\\". -> Supports the guide's instruction to use P0090 for mRCC FMT data.\\n        *   P0098 Packet: Longitudinal microbiome-immune dynamics in melanoma.\\n        *   P0284 Packet: Dual role of gut microbiome in irAEs and efficacy (P. bifermentans).\\n\\n3.  **Identify Findings:**\\n    *   **Finding 1 (Critical Contradiction):** Ch5 Outline uses P0593 for TACITO/mRCC FMT data, but `manuscript_guide` explicitly forbids this and states P0593 is about Allopurinol/Inosine. Materials (P0593 packet) confirm P0593 is Allopurinol/Inosine, not FMT/TACITO. Materials (P0090 packet) confirm P0090 contains the mRCC FMT data.\\n    *   **Finding 2 (Source Alias Handling):** `manuscript_guide` states P0333 and P0584 are the same source. The outline uses them somewhat interchangeably but sometimes separately. Need to check if the outline respects the aliasing for citation counting and consistency. In Ch3, P0584 is used for pharmacokinetics. In Ch2, P0333 is used for mechanism. This seems okay, but need to ensure they aren't double-counted in the 150 reference limit if that's tracked strictly. However, the guide says \\\"视为同一来源，避免重复计数\\\". The outline doesn't explicitly show counting, but the writing should reflect they are the same work.\\n    *   **Finding 3 (Evidence Strength/Boundary):** Ch5 Outline describes TACITO data (via P0593 incorrectly) as \\\"Phase 2a RCT\\\". The guide says mRCC FMT evidence should be from P0090 (Phase II RCT, conference abstract level). The outline's description of TACITO (12-month PFS 70% vs 41%, etc.) matches the *incorrect* attribution to P0593. The correct data (from P0090) is 1-year PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%. This needs correction to match P0090 data and attribution.\\n    *   **Finding 4 (Mechanism Distinction):** Ch3 Outline uses P0593 for Inosine mechanism (Allopurinol). This aligns with the guide. However, Ch5 uses it for FMT. This inconsistency needs fixing.\\n    *   **Finding 5 (Material Scope Limitation):** Many sources cited in the outline (e.g., P0583 for FMT-LUMINate, P0577 for MIMic, P0578 for MITRIC) are *not* in the `material_scope` (only P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284 are intact). The review must acknowledge that detailed verification of those specific trial data points (LUMINate, MIMic, MITRIC) relies on the guide's instructions and outline's claims, as the packets are missing. This is a limitation, not necessarily a finding unless there's a contradiction visible.\\n    *   **Finding 6 (Ch6 Toxicity Data):** Ch6 Outline uses P0583 for FMT-LUMINate toxicity (myocarditis 15%). P0583 is *not* in `material_scope`. The guide mentions this data in `manuscript_guide` (\\\"安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）\\\"). Since P0583 is missing from materials, I cannot verify the specific numbers, but I must note the reliance on the guide's instruction. However, the instruction in `manuscript_guide` seems to treat this as established fact for the writing. The finding should focus on the P0593/P0090 contradiction which *is* verifiable with provided materials.\\n\\n    *   **Refining Finding 1 (The P0593/TACITO Error):**\\n        *   Location: Ch5 (Chapter 5, Unit 01, Paragraph 03).\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"关于 P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...并非 TACITO 试验。正文中不得将 P0593 作为 TACITO d-FMT 联合 ICI 治疗 mRCC 的来源引用。\\\"\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \\\"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据... source_uses: P0593\\\"\\n        *   Material Evidence (P0593): \\\"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的 TME 重塑的问题... 识别出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP）...\\\"\\n        *   Material Evidence (P0090): \\\"来自 ICI 反应者的 FMT 联合 pembrolizumab + axitinib 显示出改善 PFS 和 ORR 的趋势... FMT 组 1 年 PFS 显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036）...\\\"\\n        *   Concern: Outline incorrectly attributes TACITO FMT data to P0593, contradicting the guide and material evidence.\\n        *   Proposed Change: Replace P0593 with P0090 for mRCC FMT data in Ch5, and update data points to match P0090 (1-year PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%). Move P0593 to Ch3 for Inosine/Allopurinol mechanism only.\\n\\n    *   **Refining Finding 2 (Data Consistency):**\\n        *   Location: Ch5 (Chapter 5, Unit 01, Paragraph 03).\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据（FMT 联合 pembrolizumab+axitinib，1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\\\"\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \\\"12 个月 PFS 率（70% vs 41%）与中位 PFS（24.0 vs 9.0 个月）... （P=0.053）\\\"\\n        *   Concern: The data values in the outline (70% vs 41%) differ from the guide's instructed values (66.7% vs 35.0%) which match P0090 material. This suggests the outline was drafted using the incorrect source (P0593/TACITO confusion) or different data.\\n        *   Proposed Change: Update data values to match P0090 material and guide instruction (66.7% vs 35.0%).\\n\\n    *   **Refining Finding 3 (Source Alias):**\\n        *   Location: Manuscript Guide & Outline (Ch2, Ch3, Ch5, Ch7).\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"来源别名应统一处理：P0333 与 P0584... 视为同一来源，避免重复计数\\\"\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: Ch2 uses P0333, Ch3 uses P0584, Ch5 uses P0584, Ch7 uses P0584.\\n        *   Concern: While using different handles for different contexts is okay, the writing must ensure they are not counted as distinct references in the 150 limit. The outline doesn't show the count, but the writing arrangement should note this consolidation.\\n        *   Proposed Change: Ensure writing explicitly notes P0333/P0584 identity if cited together, or consolidate handle usage in the final manuscript to avoid double counting. (This is a bit weak for a finding unless there's a visible conflict). Let's skip this as it's more about final manuscript processing than outline structure, unless the outline treats them as completely distinct works in a way that implies separate evidence bases. The outline uses them for different topics (Ch2 mechanism vs Ch3 pharmacokinetics), which is acceptable as long as the bibliography merges them. I will focus on the P0593 error which is substantive.\\n\\n    *   **Refining Finding 4 (Ch3 Inosine Context):**\\n        *   Location: Ch3 (Chapter 3, Unit 02, Paragraph 01).\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"P0593（别嘌醇/肌苷研究）在本章作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用... 其人类证据仅为小样本回顾性关联，不升级为因果。\\\"\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \\\"P0593... 发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌... 人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）中抗痛风药使用者 OS 显著优于未使用者。\\\"\\n        *   Concern: The outline correctly places P0593 in Ch3 for Inosine. However, Ch5 incorrectly uses it for FMT. The finding should focus on the Ch5 error.\\n        *   Wait, I need 6 findings max. I have one strong one (Ch5 P0593). I can split it into Attribution and Data Values.\\n        *   What about Ch6? Ch6 uses P0583 for toxicity. P0583 is not in materials. I cannot verify. But the Guide says \\\"安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）\\\". The Outline says \\\"心肌炎发生率 15%（文献报道<1%）\\\". This matches the Guide's narrative. No contradiction visible without P0583 packet.\\n        *   What about Ch1? Ch1 uses P0585 for JCOG2007. P0585 not in materials. Guide says \\\"JCOG2007 在此主讲方案特异性\\\". Outline matches.\\n        *   What about P0098? Material is present. Outline Ch6_U2_P03 uses P0098 for longitudinal data (Tregs, Bacteroides). Material confirms: \\\"基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与 Tregs 减少程度及严重 irAEs 风险正相关... 瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用\\\". Outline matches material.\\n        *   What about P0284? Material is present. Outline Ch6_U4_P01 uses P0284 for barrier/metabolite dual role. Material confirms: \\\"P. bifermentans was shown to disrupt epithelial barrier integrity in vitro... while its anti-tumor benefit was mediated by a secreted low-molecular-weight metabolite\\\". Outline matches material.\\n        *   So the main issue is P0593/P0090 in Ch5.\\n\\n    *   **Finding 2 (Ch5 Data Specifics):** The outline cites specific TACITO numbers (70% vs 41%, P=0.053) attributed to P0593. The Guide says use P0090 numbers (66.7% vs 35.0%). P0090 Material confirms 66.7% vs 35.0%. This is a data accuracy issue tied to the source attribution error.\\n    *   **Finding 3 (Ch5 Evidence Level):** Guide says P0090 data is \\\"Phase II RCT, small sample, conference abstract level\\\". Outline (Ch5_U01_P03) says \\\"Phase 2a RCT... main endpoint not statistically significant (P=0.053)\\\". This description matches the *incorrect* TACITO narrative associated with P0593 in the outline. The P0090 material says \\\"p=0.036\\\" for 1-year PFS. This is a significant statistical discrepancy (0.053 vs 0.036).\\n    *   **Finding 4 (Ch3 P0593 Context):** Guide says P0593 should be used in Ch3 as \\\"non-microbial source inosine enhancement parallel mechanism evidence\\\". Outline Ch3_U2_P01 uses P0593 for \\\"inosine targeting UBA6... P0593... allopurinol...\\\". This is correct. However, Outline Ch3_U2_P01 also lists P0582 as core evidence for UBA6. P0582 is not in materials. Guide says P0593 is for \\\"non-microbial source\\\". P0582 is \\\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine\\\". The outline distinguishes them. This seems okay.\\n    *   **Finding 5 (Material Scope Blind Spot):** Many key trial sources (P0583, P0577, P0578) cited in Ch1, Ch5, Ch6 are not in `material_scope`. The review cannot verify their specific data points (e.g., LUMINate ORR 80%, MITRIC ORR 0%). This must be stated in limitations.\\n    *   **Finding 6 (Source Alias P0049/P0605):** Guide says \\\"P0049 与 P0605 等视为同一来源\\\". Outline Ch6_U1_P03 uses P0049 and P0605 separately for limitations (sample size). Ch6_U2_P03 uses P0049 and P0605 for development. This is acceptable usage as long as they aren't double counted in references. I will note this in limitations or a finding if there's a risk of double counting in the text. Let's look for a better finding.\\n    *   **Finding 6 (Ch4 PPI Data):** Ch4_U02_P01 uses P0339 for PPI Meta-analysis (OS HR 1.31). P0339 is not in materials. Guide says \\\"P0339 与 P0584 等视为同一来源\\\" (Wait, Guide says P0333 & P0584, P0402 & P0576, P0049 & P0605). P0339 is not aliased in the guide excerpt provided. However, P0339 is not in materials. I can't verify.\\n    *   **Finding 6 (Ch1 Evidence Ladder):** Ch1_U4 requires a table comparing trials (FMT-LUMINate, MITRIC, MIMic). Sources P0583, P0578, P0577 are not in materials. I must note this limitation.\\n\\n    *   **Decision:** I will focus on the P0593/P0090 contradiction in Ch5 as the primary findings (split into Attribution, Data Values, and Statistical Significance). Then I will address the Material Scope limitations regarding other key trials.\\n\\n    *   **Drafting Findings:**\\n        1.  **Ch5 Source Attribution:** P0593 used for TACITO/FMT, Guide says P0593 is Allopurinol/Inosine, P0090 is FMT. Material confirms.\\n        2.  **Ch5 Data Values:** Outline uses 70%/41%, Guide/P0090 Material uses 66.7%/35.0%.\\n        3.  **Ch5 Statistical Significance:** Outline uses P=0.053 (TACITO narrative), P0090 Material uses p=0.036.\\n        4.  **Ch3 P0593 Context:** Ensure P0593 is restricted to Ch3 (Inosine) and not Ch5 (FMT). (This is part of finding 1 essentially).\\n        5.  **Material Scope (Trials):** P0583, P0577, P0578 missing. Cannot verify LUMINate/MIMic/MITRIC data.\\n        6.  **Material Scope (Meta-analyses):** P0081, P0339, P0402 missing. Cannot verify antibiotic/PPI effect sizes.\\n\\n    *   **Refining for \\\"Locally Repairable\\\":**\\n        *   Finding 1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution.\\n        *   Finding 2: Ch5 Data Values (70% vs 66.7%).\\n        *   Finding 3: Ch5 P-value (0.053 vs 0.036).\\n        *   Finding 4: Ch3 P0593 Description (Ensure it emphasizes non-microbial/Allopurinol).\\n        *   Finding 5: Limitation on P0583/P0577/P0578.\\n        *   Finding 6: Limitation on P0081/P0339.\\n\\n    *   **Wait, I need to check if P0593 is used in Ch3 correctly.**\\n        *   Ch3_U2_P01: \\\"P0593... 发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...\\\". This matches the Guide and Material.\\n        *   Ch5_U01_P03: \\\"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据... source_uses: P0593\\\". This is the error.\\n        *   So Finding 1 covers the Ch5 error. Finding 2 covers the data values. Finding 3 covers the p-value.\\n        *   Finding 4: Ch6 uses P0583 for toxicity. P0583 not in materials. Guide mentions the finding (Prevotella/myocarditis) in `manuscript_guide`. This is a limitation.\\n        *   Finding 5: Ch1 Table requires P0583, P0577, P0578. Not in materials. Limitation.\\n        *   Finding 6: Source Aliasing (P0333/P0584, P0049/P0605). The outline uses them in different chapters. Need to ensure the final text merges them in the reference list. This is a writing arrangement issue.\\n\\n    *   **Consolidating:**\\n        *   F1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution Error (Guide + P0593 Material + P0090 Material).\\n        *   F2: Ch5 Data Discrepancy (70%/41% vs 66.7%/35.0%).\\n        *   F3: Ch5 Statistical Significance (P=0.053 vs p=0.036).\\n        *   F4: Ch3 P0593 Context (Ensure it remains parallel mechanism, not FMT).\\n        *   F5: Limitation on Missing Trial Data (P0583, P0577, P0578).\\n        *   F6: Limitation on Missing Meta-analysis Data (P0081, P0339).\\n\\n    *   **Wait, I need to make sure I don't exceed 6 findings.** I will combine F1, F2, F3 into one strong finding about Ch5 P0593/P0090 confusion, or split them if they represent distinct repair actions. The guide says \\\"Prefer a small local correction over a global rewrite.\\\" Correcting the source handle is one action. Correcting the numbers is another. Correcting the p-value is another. I'll split F1 (Source) and F2 (Data/Stats).\\n    *   Actually, F1 (Source) implies F2 (Data). If I change the source to P0090, I must change the data. I can combine them into one finding about Ch5_U01_P03.\\n    *   Let's look for other issues.\\n    *   Ch1_U4 Table: Requires P0583, P0577, P0578. These are missing from materials. I can't verify the ORR values (80%, 65%, 0%). I must state this in limitations.\\n    *   Ch6_U3_P01: Uses P0583 for toxicity. Missing from materials. Limitation.\\n    *   Ch4_U01_P01: Uses P0575 for antibiotic timing. Missing from materials. Limitation.\\n    *   Ch2_U01_P01: Uses P0080 for LPS. Missing from materials. Limitation.\\n    *   Okay, most specific data points rely on missing materials. The *only* verifiable contradiction is P0593/P0090 in Ch5 because both are in materials (P0593, P0090) AND the Guide explicitly corrects this.\\n    *   So I will focus my findings on the P0593/P0090 issue (split into Source Attribution and Data Consistency) and the Material Scope limitations.\\n    *   Finding 1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution (Guide + P0593 Material vs Outline).\\n    *   Finding 2: Ch5 Data Values (P0090 Material vs Outline).\\n    *   Finding 3: Ch5 P-value (P0090 Material vs Outline).\\n    *   Finding 4: Ch3 P0593 Description (Ensure it doesn't imply FMT).\\n    *   Finding 5: Limitation on P0583/P0577/P0578 (Ch1/Ch5/Ch6).\\n    *   Finding 6: Limitation on P0081/P0339/P0575 (Ch1/Ch4).\\n\\n    *   Wait, I need to check if P0090 is in materials. Yes, `materials` list includes P0090.\\n    *   I need to check if P0593 is in materials. Yes, `materials` list includes P0593.\\n    *   So I have evidence for F1, F2, F3.\\n    *   F4 is redundant if F1 is fixed.\\n    *   F5, F6 are limitations.\\n    *   I need 0-6 findings. I can have 3 findings and 3 limitations.\\n    *   Let's create 3 findings around the Ch5 error (Source, Data, Stats) and 3 limitations around missing materials.\\n    *   Actually, combining Source + Data + Stats into one finding is better because they are all about the same paragraph (Ch5_U01_P03). I'll make that F1.\\n    *   F2: Ch3 P0593 usage. The outline uses it correctly in Ch3, but I should ensure the description matches the material (Allopurinol/Inosine, not microbiome-derived). The outline says \\\"别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌\\\". This matches. No finding needed here unless there's a nuance. The Guide says \\\"P0593 应在 Ch3 肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用\\\". Outline says \\\"P0593... 例证... 发现别嘌醇...\\\". This is compliant.\\n    *   F2: Source Aliasing (P0333/P0584, P0049/P0605). The outline uses them in different places. I should note that the final text must merge them to avoid double counting in the 150 ref limit.\\n    *   F3: Ch1 Table Data (P0583, P0577, P0578). Since materials are missing, I can't verify. But the Guide gives specific instructions for Ch1 Table (\\\"至少包括 FMT-LUMINate、MITRIC、MIMic...\\\"). The Outline matches this. No contradiction, just unverifiable. This goes to limitations.\\n    *   So I have 1 strong finding (Ch5 P0593/P0090). I need more findings if possible.\\n    *   Check Ch6_U3_P01: Uses P0583 for toxicity (Myocarditis 15%). Guide says \\\"安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）\\\". Outline says \\\"心肌炎发生率 15%（文献报道<1%）\\\". This matches the Guide's narrative. No contradiction.\\n    *   Check Ch4_U02_P01: Uses P0339 for PPI HR 1.31. P0339 not in materials. Guide doesn't specify the HR value, just says \\\"PPI 部分...\\\".\\n    *   Okay, I will focus on the Ch5 error as the main finding (maybe split into Source and Data for clarity). And use Limitations for the rest.\\n    *   Wait, I can create a finding about the `manuscript_guide` instruction vs `full_outline` structure regarding P0593.\\n    *   Finding 1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution.\\n    *   Finding 2: Ch5 Data Values (P0090 vs Outline).\\n    *   Finding 3: Ch5 P-value (P0090 vs Outline).\\n    *   Finding 4: Source Alias Handling (P0333/P0584).\\n    *   Finding 5: Limitation on P0583/P0577/P0578.\\n    *   Finding 6: Limitation on P0081/P0339.\\n    *   This works.\\n\\n    *   **Refining Finding 4 (Aliases):** The guide says \\\"P0333 与 P0584... 视为同一来源\\\". The outline uses P0333 in Ch2 and P0584 in Ch3/Ch5/Ch7. This is acceptable for navigation, but the writing must ensure they are not counted twice. I will frame this as a writing arrangement concern.\\n\\n    *   **Refining Limitations:**\\n        *   L1: P0583 (FMT-LUMINate) missing.\\n        *   L2: P0577 (MIMic) missing.\\n        *   L3: P0578 (MITRIC) missing.\\n        *   L4: P0081 (Antibiotic Meta) missing.\\n        *   L5: P0339 (PPI Meta) missing.\\n        *   L6: P0575 (Antibiotic Timing) missing.\\n        *   L7: P0098 (Longitudinal) is present, but P0090/P0593 are the only ones fully verifiable for the Ch5 conflict.\\n        *   I'll group the missing trial sources into one limitation and missing meta-analyses into another.\\n\\n4.  **Constructing JSON:**\\n    *   Ensure all strings are <= 1200 chars.\\n    *   Ensure JSON is valid.\\n    *   Ensure language is Chinese.\\n    *   Ensure `evidence_excerpt` comes from the provided input strings (Guide, Outline, or Materials).\\n\\n    *   **Finding 1 (Ch5 Source):**\\n        *   Location: Ch5\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"关于 P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...并非 TACITO 试验。正文中不得将 P0593 作为 TACITO d-FMT 联合 ICI 治疗 mRCC 的来源引用。\\\"\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \\\"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据... source_uses: P0593\\\"\\n        *   Material Excerpt (P0593): \\\"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的 TME 重塑的问题... 识别出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP）...\\\"\\n        *   Concern: Outline attributes TACITO/FMT data to P0593, contradicting Guide and Material.\\n        *   Change: Use P0090 for mRCC FMT data in Ch5.\\n        *   Evidence Basis: guide, outline, materials.\\n\\n    *   **Finding 2 (Ch5 Data):**\\n        *   Location: Ch5\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据（FMT 联合 pembrolizumab+axitinib，1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\\\"\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \\\"12 个月 PFS 率（70% vs 41%）与中位 PFS（24.0 vs 9.0 个月）\\\"\\n        *   Material Excerpt (P0090): \\\"FMT 组 1 年 PFS 显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036）\\\"\\n        *   Concern: Data values differ.\\n        *   Change: Update to 66.7% vs 35.0%.\\n        *   Evidence Basis: guide, outline, materials.\\n\\n    *   **Finding 3 (Ch5 Stats):**\\n        *   Location: Ch5\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据... 1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%（p=0.036）\\\" (Wait, Guide doesn't explicitly state p=0.036, it says \\\"1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%\\\". P0090 Material says p=0.036. Outline says P=0.053).\\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \\\"主要终点未达统计学显著性（P=0.053）\\\"\\n        *   Material Excerpt (P0090): \\\"1 年 PFS 显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036）\\\"\\n        *   Concern: P-value discrepancy (0.053 vs 0.036).\\n        *   Change: Update to p=0.036 and note significance.\\n        *   Evidence Basis: outline, materials. (Guide implies P0090 is the source, Material provides the stat).\\n\\n    *   **Finding 4 (Source Alias):**\\n        *   Location: manuscript_guide\\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \\\"来源别名应统一处理：P0333 与 P0584、P0402 与 P0576、P0049 与 P\"}}],\"id\":\"chatcmpl-5d6abef9-77c0-9905-a8f8-4b997e43e0d0\",\"model\":\"qwen3.5-plus\",\"usage\":{\"completion_tokens\":11160,\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":8192,\"text_tokens\":11160},\"prompt_tokens\":268593,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"text_tokens\":268593},\"total_tokens\":279753}}",
  "raw_stream_sha256": "3eb4ba62edeb4724d9442fa855f2044397ca2b39c631d416e7c25b6468aa7318",
  "reasoning_content": "Thinking Process:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Request:**\n    *   **Role:** Independent, one-pass reviewer of a complete writing GUIDE (not a grader or manuscript author).\n    *   **Task:** Read the original guide, full outline, and light catalog. Scientific source packets are intact but may cover only part of the catalog. Check `material_scope` and acknowledge blind spots. A catalog clue is navigation, not evidence. Do not invent material readings, scientific claims, references, or missing draft context.\n    *   **Output:** One JSON object with exactly `findings` (array, 0-6 items) and `limitations` (array, 0-8 items). No Markdown outside JSON.\n    *   **Constraints:**\n        *   Findings must have specific fields (`id`, `location`, `guide_excerpt`, `concern`, `proposed_change`, `evidence_basis`, `evidence_excerpt`).\n        *   Strings max 1200 chars.\n        *   Total JSON < 20,000 UTF-8 bytes.\n        *   Focus on important omissions, avoidable repetition, misplaced discussion, unclear comparison conditions, evidence strength/boundaries, feasible writing arrangements.\n        *   Prefer small local correction over global rewrite.\n        *   Claims outside visible material must be stated as limitations, not invented factual corrections.\n        *   Use original guide's language (Chinese).\n        *   Prioritize lost independent explanations, comparisons, counterexamples, conditions, source handoffs.\n        *   Do not impose new fixed templates or generic defensive disclaimers.\n\n2.  **Analyze the Inputs:**\n    *   **Original Guide (`original_guide`):** Contains `manuscript_guide` (overall structure, citation rules, specific source handling like P0593 vs TACITO), and `chapters` (Ch1-Ch7 with `writing_arrangement` and `required_content`).\n    *   **Full Outline (`full_outline`):** Contains detailed chapter frames, units, paragraph tasks, source uses, etc.\n    *   **Source Catalog (`source_catalog`):** List of sources (P0096, P0146, etc.) with identities and content clues.\n    *   **Materials (`materials`):** Intact packets for P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284.\n    *   **Material Scope:** Includes P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284. Omits many others (P0583, P0577, P0578, P0081, etc.).\n    *   **Key Instruction in `manuscript_guide`:**\n        *   \"关于 P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...并非 TACITO 试验。正文中不得将 P0593 作为 TACITO d-FMT 联合 ICI 治疗 mRCC 的来源引用。P0593 应在 Ch3 肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用...mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据...\"\n        *   \"来源别名应统一处理：P0333 与 P0584、P0402 与 P0576、P0049 与 P0605 等视为同一来源...\"\n        *   Ch5 `required_content`: \"mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据引用 P0090 汇总数据（1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%，ORR 54% vs 28%），标注为 Phase II RCT、小样本、会议摘要级别。不使用 P0593 作为此数据来源。\"\n    *   **Full Outline Ch5 Content:**\n        *   Ch5_U01_P03: \"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据...说明 d-FMT 组在 mRCC 一线治疗中 12 个月 PFS 率（70% vs 41%）与中位 PFS（24.0 vs 9.0 个月）呈有利趋势，但主要终点未达统计学显著性（P=0.053）... source_uses: P0593\".\n        *   This directly contradicts the `manuscript_guide` instruction regarding P0593. The guide says P0593 is *not* TACITO and should not be used for mRCC FMT data. The outline uses P0593 for TACITO mRCC FMT data.\n    *   **Materials Check:**\n        *   P0593 Packet: Confirms it is about Allopurinol/Inosine, *not* TACITO/FMT. \"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的 TME 重塑的问题... 识别出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP）... 一项包含 50 名膀胱癌患者的回顾性研究显示，接受抗痛风药物治疗的患者在抗 PD-1 治疗下的总生存期显著优于未使用者。\" -> Supports the guide's warning.\n        *   P0090 Packet: Confirms it is a systematic review including mRCC FMT data. \"来自 ICI 反应者的 FMT 联合 pembrolizumab + axitinib 显示出改善 PFS 和 ORR 的趋势... FMT 组 1 年 PFS 显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036），ORR 提高（54% vs 28%）... 基于 Phase II RCT 摘要，n=50\". -> Supports the guide's instruction to use P0090 for mRCC FMT data.\n        *   P0098 Packet: Longitudinal microbiome-immune dynamics in melanoma.\n        *   P0284 Packet: Dual role of gut microbiome in irAEs and efficacy (P. bifermentans).\n\n3.  **Identify Findings:**\n    *   **Finding 1 (Critical Contradiction):** Ch5 Outline uses P0593 for TACITO/mRCC FMT data, but `manuscript_guide` explicitly forbids this and states P0593 is about Allopurinol/Inosine. Materials (P0593 packet) confirm P0593 is Allopurinol/Inosine, not FMT/TACITO. Materials (P0090 packet) confirm P0090 contains the mRCC FMT data.\n    *   **Finding 2 (Source Alias Handling):** `manuscript_guide` states P0333 and P0584 are the same source. The outline uses them somewhat interchangeably but sometimes separately. Need to check if the outline respects the aliasing for citation counting and consistency. In Ch3, P0584 is used for pharmacokinetics. In Ch2, P0333 is used for mechanism. This seems okay, but need to ensure they aren't double-counted in the 150 reference limit if that's tracked strictly. However, the guide says \"视为同一来源，避免重复计数\". The outline doesn't explicitly show counting, but the writing should reflect they are the same work.\n    *   **Finding 3 (Evidence Strength/Boundary):** Ch5 Outline describes TACITO data (via P0593 incorrectly) as \"Phase 2a RCT\". The guide says mRCC FMT evidence should be from P0090 (Phase II RCT, conference abstract level). The outline's description of TACITO (12-month PFS 70% vs 41%, etc.) matches the *incorrect* attribution to P0593. The correct data (from P0090) is 1-year PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%. This needs correction to match P0090 data and attribution.\n    *   **Finding 4 (Mechanism Distinction):** Ch3 Outline uses P0593 for Inosine mechanism (Allopurinol). This aligns with the guide. However, Ch5 uses it for FMT. This inconsistency needs fixing.\n    *   **Finding 5 (Material Scope Limitation):** Many sources cited in the outline (e.g., P0583 for FMT-LUMINate, P0577 for MIMic, P0578 for MITRIC) are *not* in the `material_scope` (only P0098, P0593, P0090, P0284 are intact). The review must acknowledge that detailed verification of those specific trial data points (LUMINate, MIMic, MITRIC) relies on the guide's instructions and outline's claims, as the packets are missing. This is a limitation, not necessarily a finding unless there's a contradiction visible.\n    *   **Finding 6 (Ch6 Toxicity Data):** Ch6 Outline uses P0583 for FMT-LUMINate toxicity (myocarditis 15%). P0583 is *not* in `material_scope`. The guide mentions this data in `manuscript_guide` (\"安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）\"). Since P0583 is missing from materials, I cannot verify the specific numbers, but I must note the reliance on the guide's instruction. However, the instruction in `manuscript_guide` seems to treat this as established fact for the writing. The finding should focus on the P0593/P0090 contradiction which *is* verifiable with provided materials.\n\n    *   **Refining Finding 1 (The P0593/TACITO Error):**\n        *   Location: Ch5 (Chapter 5, Unit 01, Paragraph 03).\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \"关于 P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...并非 TACITO 试验。正文中不得将 P0593 作为 TACITO d-FMT 联合 ICI 治疗 mRCC 的来源引用。\"\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据... source_uses: P0593\"\n        *   Material Evidence (P0593): \"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的 TME 重塑的问题... 识别出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP）...\"\n        *   Material Evidence (P0090): \"来自 ICI 反应者的 FMT 联合 pembrolizumab + axitinib 显示出改善 PFS 和 ORR 的趋势... FMT 组 1 年 PFS 显著高于对照组（66.7% vs 35.0%, p=0.036）...\"\n        *   Concern: Outline incorrectly attributes TACITO FMT data to P0593, contradicting the guide and material evidence.\n        *   Proposed Change: Replace P0593 with P0090 for mRCC FMT data in Ch5, and update data points to match P0090 (1-year PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%). Move P0593 to Ch3 for Inosine/Allopurinol mechanism only.\n\n    *   **Refining Finding 2 (Data Consistency):**\n        *   Location: Ch5 (Chapter 5, Unit 01, Paragraph 03).\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \"mRCC 中 FMT 联合 ICI 的随机证据应引用 P0090 系统综述中汇总的 Phase II RCT 数据（FMT 联合 pembrolizumab+axitinib，1 年 PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\"\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \"12 个月 PFS 率（70% vs 41%）与中位 PFS（24.0 vs 9.0 个月）... （P=0.053）\"\n        *   Concern: The data values in the outline (70% vs 41%) differ from the guide's instructed values (66.7% vs 35.0%) which match P0090 material. This suggests the outline was drafted using the incorrect source (P0593/TACITO confusion) or different data.\n        *   Proposed Change: Update data values to match P0090 material and guide instruction (66.7% vs 35.0%).\n\n    *   **Refining Finding 3 (Source Alias):**\n        *   Location: Manuscript Guide & Outline (Ch2, Ch3, Ch5, Ch7).\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \"来源别名应统一处理：P0333 与 P0584... 视为同一来源，避免重复计数\"\n        *   Outline Excerpt: Ch2 uses P0333, Ch3 uses P0584, Ch5 uses P0584, Ch7 uses P0584.\n        *   Concern: While using different handles for different contexts is okay, the writing must ensure they are not counted as distinct references in the 150 limit. The outline doesn't show the count, but the writing arrangement should note this consolidation.\n        *   Proposed Change: Ensure writing explicitly notes P0333/P0584 identity if cited together, or consolidate handle usage in the final manuscript to avoid double counting. (This is a bit weak for a finding unless there's a visible conflict). Let's skip this as it's more about final manuscript processing than outline structure, unless the outline treats them as completely distinct works in a way that implies separate evidence bases. The outline uses them for different topics (Ch2 mechanism vs Ch3 pharmacokinetics), which is acceptable as long as the bibliography merges them. I will focus on the P0593 error which is substantive.\n\n    *   **Refining Finding 4 (Ch3 Inosine Context):**\n        *   Location: Ch3 (Chapter 3, Unit 02, Paragraph 01).\n        *   Guide Excerpt: \"P0593（别嘌醇/肌苷研究）在本章作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用... 其人类证据仅为小样本回顾性关联，不升级为因果。\"\n        *   Outline Excerpt: \"P0593... 发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌... 人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）中抗痛风药使用者 OS 显著优于未使用者。\"\n        *   Concern: The outline correctly places P0593 in Ch3 for Inosine. However, Ch5 incorrectly uses it for FMT. The finding should focus on the Ch5 error.\n        *   Wait, I need 6 findings max. I have one strong one (Ch5 P0593). I can split it into Attribution and Data Values.\n        *   What about Ch6? Ch6 uses P0583 for toxicity. P0583 is not in materials. I cannot verify. But the Guide says \"安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）\". The Outline says \"心肌炎发生率 15%（文献报道<1%）\". This matches the Guide's narrative. No contradiction visible without P0583 packet.\n        *   What about Ch1? Ch1 uses P0585 for JCOG2007. P0585 not in materials. Guide says \"JCOG2007 在此主讲方案特异性\". Outline matches.\n        *   What about P0098? Material is present. Outline Ch6_U2_P03 uses P0098 for longitudinal data (Tregs, Bacteroides). Material confirms: \"基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与 Tregs 减少程度及严重 irAEs 风险正相关... 瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用\". Outline matches material.\n        *   What about P0284? Material is present. Outline Ch6_U4_P01 uses P0284 for barrier/metabolite dual role. Material confirms: \"P. bifermentans was shown to disrupt epithelial barrier integrity in vitro... while its anti-tumor benefit was mediated by a secreted low-molecular-weight metabolite\". Outline matches material.\n        *   So the main issue is P0593/P0090 in Ch5.\n\n    *   **Finding 2 (Ch5 Data Specifics):** The outline cites specific TACITO numbers (70% vs 41%, P=0.053) attributed to P0593. The Guide says use P0090 numbers (66.7% vs 35.0%). P0090 Material confirms 66.7% vs 35.0%. This is a data accuracy issue tied to the source attribution error.\n    *   **Finding 3 (Ch5 Evidence Level):** Guide says P0090 data is \"Phase II RCT, small sample, conference abstract level\". Outline (Ch5_U01_P03) says \"Phase 2a RCT... main endpoint not statistically significant (P=0.053)\". This description matches the *incorrect* TACITO narrative associated with P0593 in the outline. The P0090 material says \"p=0.036\" for 1-year PFS. This is a significant statistical discrepancy (0.053 vs 0.036).\n    *   **Finding 4 (Ch3 P0593 Context):** Guide says P0593 should be used in Ch3 as \"non-microbial source inosine enhancement parallel mechanism evidence\". Outline Ch3_U2_P01 uses P0593 for \"inosine targeting UBA6... P0593... allopurinol...\". This is correct. However, Outline Ch3_U2_P01 also lists P0582 as core evidence for UBA6. P0582 is not in materials. Guide says P0593 is for \"non-microbial source\". P0582 is \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine\". The outline distinguishes them. This seems okay.\n    *   **Finding 5 (Material Scope Blind Spot):** Many key trial sources (P0583, P0577, P0578) cited in Ch1, Ch5, Ch6 are not in `material_scope`. The review cannot verify their specific data points (e.g., LUMINate ORR 80%, MITRIC ORR 0%). This must be stated in limitations.\n    *   **Finding 6 (Source Alias P0049/P0605):** Guide says \"P0049 与 P0605 等视为同一来源\". Outline Ch6_U1_P03 uses P0049 and P0605 separately for limitations (sample size). Ch6_U2_P03 uses P0049 and P0605 for development. This is acceptable usage as long as they aren't double counted in references. I will note this in limitations or a finding if there's a risk of double counting in the text. Let's look for a better finding.\n    *   **Finding 6 (Ch4 PPI Data):** Ch4_U02_P01 uses P0339 for PPI Meta-analysis (OS HR 1.31). P0339 is not in materials. Guide says \"P0339 与 P0584 等视为同一来源\" (Wait, Guide says P0333 & P0584, P0402 & P0576, P0049 & P0605). P0339 is not aliased in the guide excerpt provided. However, P0339 is not in materials. I can't verify.\n    *   **Finding 6 (Ch1 Evidence Ladder):** Ch1_U4 requires a table comparing trials (FMT-LUMINate, MITRIC, MIMic). Sources P0583, P0578, P0577 are not in materials. I must note this limitation.\n\n    *   **Decision:** I will focus on the P0593/P0090 contradiction in Ch5 as the primary findings (split into Attribution, Data Values, and Statistical Significance). Then I will address the Material Scope limitations regarding other key trials.\n\n    *   **Drafting Findings:**\n        1.  **Ch5 Source Attribution:** P0593 used for TACITO/FMT, Guide says P0593 is Allopurinol/Inosine, P0090 is FMT. Material confirms.\n        2.  **Ch5 Data Values:** Outline uses 70%/41%, Guide/P0090 Material uses 66.7%/35.0%.\n        3.  **Ch5 Statistical Significance:** Outline uses P=0.053 (TACITO narrative), P0090 Material uses p=0.036.\n        4.  **Ch3 P0593 Context:** Ensure P0593 is restricted to Ch3 (Inosine) and not Ch5 (FMT). (This is part of finding 1 essentially).\n        5.  **Material Scope (Trials):** P0583, P0577, P0578 missing. Cannot verify LUMINate/MIMic/MITRIC data.\n        6.  **Material Scope (Meta-analyses):** P0081, P0339, P0402 missing. Cannot verify antibiotic/PPI effect sizes.\n\n    *   **Refining for \"Locally Repairable\":**\n        *   Finding 1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution.\n        *   Finding 2: Ch5 Data Values (70% vs 66.7%).\n        *   Finding 3: Ch5 P-value (0.053 vs 0.036).\n        *   Finding 4: Ch3 P0593 Description (Ensure it emphasizes non-microbial/Allopurinol).\n        *   Finding 5: Limitation on P0583/P0577/P0578.\n        *   Finding 6: Limitation on P0081/P0339.\n\n    *   **Wait, I need to check if P0593 is used in Ch3 correctly.**\n        *   Ch3_U2_P01: \"P0593... 发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌...\". This matches the Guide and Material.\n        *   Ch5_U01_P03: \"引入 TACITO Phase 2a RCT 数据... source_uses: P0593\". This is the error.\n        *   So Finding 1 covers the Ch5 error. Finding 2 covers the data values. Finding 3 covers the p-value.\n        *   Finding 4: Ch6 uses P0583 for toxicity. P0583 not in materials. Guide mentions the finding (Prevotella/myocarditis) in `manuscript_guide`. This is a limitation.\n        *   Finding 5: Ch1 Table requires P0583, P0577, P0578. Not in materials. Limitation.\n        *   Finding 6: Source Aliasing (P0333/P0584, P0049/P0605). The outline uses them in different chapters. Need to ensure the final text merges them in the reference list. This is a writing arrangement issue.\n\n    *   **Consolidating:**\n        *   F1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution Error (Guide + P0593 Material + P0090 Material).\n        *   F2: Ch5 Data Discrepancy (70%/41% vs 66.7%/35.0%).\n        *   F3: Ch5 Statistical Significance (P=0.053 vs p=0.036).\n        *   F4: Ch3 P0593 Context (Ensure it remains parallel mechanism, not FMT).\n        *   F5: Limitation on Missing Trial Data (P0583, P0577, P0578).\n        *   F6: Limitation on Missing Meta-analysis Data (P0081, P0339).\n\n    *   **Wait, I need to make sure I don't exceed 6 findings.** I will combine F1, F2, F3 into one strong finding about Ch5 P0593/P0090 confusion, or split them if they represent distinct repair actions. The guide says \"Prefer a small local correction over a global rewrite.\" Correcting the source handle is one action. Correcting the numbers is another. Correcting the p-value is another. I'll split F1 (Source) and F2 (Data/Stats).\n    *   Actually, F1 (Source) implies F2 (Data). If I change the source to P0090, I must change the data. I can combine them into one finding about Ch5_U01_P03.\n    *   Let's look for other issues.\n    *   Ch1_U4 Table: Requires P0583, P0577, P0578. These are missing from materials. I can't verify the ORR values (80%, 65%, 0%). I must state this in limitations.\n    *   Ch6_U3_P01: Uses P0583 for toxicity. Missing from materials. Limitation.\n    *   Ch4_U01_P01: Uses P0575 for antibiotic timing. Missing from materials. Limitation.\n    *   Ch2_U01_P01: Uses P0080 for LPS. Missing from materials. Limitation.\n    *   Okay, most specific data points rely on missing materials. The *only* verifiable contradiction is P0593/P0090 in Ch5 because both are in materials (P0593, P0090) AND the Guide explicitly corrects this.\n    *   So I will focus my findings on the P0593/P0090 issue (split into Source Attribution and Data Consistency) and the Material Scope limitations.\n    *   Finding 1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution (Guide + P0593 Material vs Outline).\n    *   Finding 2: Ch5 Data Values (P0090 Material vs Outline).\n    *   Finding 3: Ch5 P-value (P0090 Material vs Outline).\n    *   Finding 4: Ch3 P0593 Description (Ensure it doesn't imply FMT).\n    *   Finding 5: Limitation on P0583/P0577/P0578 (Ch1/Ch5/Ch6).\n    *   Finding 6: Limitation on P0081/P0339/P0575 (Ch1/Ch4).\n\n    *   Wait, I need to check if P0090 is in materials. Yes, `materials` list includes P0090.\n    *   I need to check if P0593 is in materials. Yes, `materials` list includes P0593.\n    *   So I have evidence for F1, F2, F3.\n    *   F4 is redundant if F1 is fixed.\n    *   F5, F6 are limitations.\n    *   I need 0-6 findings. I can have 3 findings and 3 limitations.\n    *   Let's create 3 findings around the Ch5 error (Source, Data, Stats) and 3 limitations around missing materials.\n    *   Actually, combining Source + Data + Stats into one finding is better because they are all about the same paragraph (Ch5_U01_P03). I'll make that F1.\n    *   F2: Ch3 P0593 usage. The outline uses it correctly in Ch3, but I should ensure the description matches the material (Allopurinol/Inosine, not microbiome-derived). The outline says \"别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌\". This matches. No finding needed here unless there's a nuance. The Guide says \"P0593 应在 Ch3 肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用\". Outline says \"P0593... 例证... 发现别嘌醇...\". This is compliant.\n    *   F2: Source Aliasing (P0333/P0584, P0049/P0605). The outline uses them in different places. I should note that the final text must merge them to avoid double counting in the 150 ref limit.\n    *   F3: Ch1 Table Data (P0583, P0577, P0578). Since materials are missing, I can't verify. But the Guide gives specific instructions for Ch1 Table (\"至少包括 FMT-LUMINate、MITRIC、MIMic...\"). The Outline matches this. No contradiction, just unverifiable. This goes to limitations.\n    *   So I have 1 strong finding (Ch5 P0593/P0090). I need more findings if possible.\n    *   Check Ch6_U3_P01: Uses P0583 for toxicity (Myocarditis 15%). Guide says \"安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）\". Outline says \"心肌炎发生率 15%（文献报道<1%）\". This matches the Guide's narrative. No contradiction.\n    *   Check Ch4_U02_P01: Uses P0339 for PPI HR 1.31. P0339 not in materials. Guide doesn't specify the HR value, just says \"PPI 部分...\".\n    *   Okay, I will focus on the Ch5 error as the main finding (maybe split into Source and Data for clarity). And use Limitations for the rest.\n    *   Wait, I can create a finding about the `manuscript_guide` instruction vs `full_outline` structure regarding P0593.\n    *   Finding 1: Ch5 P0593 Attribution.\n    *   Finding 2: Ch5 Data Values (P0090 vs Outline).\n    *   Finding 3: Ch5 P-value (P0090 vs Outline).\n    *   Finding 4: Source Alias Handling (P0333/P0584).\n    *   Finding 5: Limitation on P0583/P0577/P0578.\n    *   Finding 6: Limitation on P0081/P0339.\n    *   This works.\n\n    *   **Refining Finding 4 (Aliases):** The guide says \"P0333 与 P0584... 视为同一来源\". The outline uses P0333 in Ch2 and P0584 in Ch3/Ch5/Ch7. This is acceptable for navigation, but the writing must ensure they are not counted twice. I will frame this as a writing arrangement concern.\n\n    *   **Refining Limitations:**\n        *   L1: P0583 (FMT-LUMINate) missing.\n        *   L2: P0577 (MIMic) missing.\n        *   L3: P0578 (MITRIC) missing.\n        *   L4: P0081 (Antibiotic Meta) missing.\n        *   L5: P0339 (PPI Meta) missing.\n        *   L6: P0575 (Antibiotic Timing) missing.\n        *   L7: P0098 (Longitudinal) is present, but P0090/P0593 are the only ones fully verifiable for the Ch5 conflict.\n        *   I'll group the missing trial sources into one limitation and missing meta-analyses into another.\n\n4.  **Constructing JSON:**\n    *   Ensure all strings are <= 1200 chars.\n    *   Ensure JSON is valid.\n    *   Ensure language is Chinese.\n    *   Ensure `evidence_excerpt` comes from the provided input strings (Guide, 